    "result_text": "The suite is exactly these tests (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract, `AuditLogCapture` is a helper), so the full suite is the 2 acceptance tests \u2014 both green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `membershipTier` on the owner response: **`SILVER`** when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise **`BRONZE`**.\n\nThe tier is a derived, read-only field (no DB column needed \u2014 it's computed from already-stored fields), so I added it in two places:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipTier` property (string, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto(Owner)` deriving the value:\n   ```java\n   (owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n        && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty()) ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n   ```\n\nBecause both `GET /api/owners/{id}` (`RespondWithOwner`) and the create/update responders map through `toOwnerDto`, the field surfaces consistently. `namesakeCount` was already wired end-to-end via `AssignNamesakeCount`, so no changes were needed there.\n\n**Result:** `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
